==Description==

The [[Image:Silk_SilkPose.svg|32px]] '''Silk SilkPose''' command creates a SilkPose object, a support with a 3D placement calculated from linked references, intended to attach sketches.

</translate>
[[Image:Silk_SilkPose-01.png|400px]]
<translate>

{{Caption|A SilkPose object on a surface corner (the long line represents its x-axis the short one its y-axis)}}

==Usage==

# There are several options to select elements in the [[3D_View|3D View]]:
#* Select 1 vertex. Uses the parent object's placement for orientation, sets PR mode.
#* Select 1 vertex and an element belonging to an object that has a placement to use for orientation, sets PR mode.
#* Select 3 vertices of 1, 2, or 3 objects. Derives the orientation from the vertices, sets 3P mode.
# There are several ways to invoke the command.
#* Press the {{Button|[[Image:Silk_SilkPose.svg|16px]] SilkPose}} button.
#* Select the {{MenuCommand|Silk → [[Image:Silk_SilkPose.svg|16px]] SilkPose}} option from the menu.
# One of the following objects is created:
#* A '''SilkPose_PR''' object if the first or second selection option was chosen.
#* A '''SilkPose_3P''' object if the third selection option was chosen.

== Properties ==

See also: [[Property_View|Property View]].

All '''SilkPose''' objects are derived from a [[Part_Feature|Part feature]], or more precise a {{Incode|Part::FeaturePython}} object, and inherit all its properties. They also have the following common additional properties:

=== Data ===

{{Properties_Title|C3 - Identifiers}}

* {{PropertyData|internalName|String}}: The permanent internal FreeCAD name for this object.
* {{PropertyData|object_version|String}}: The class version of this object.


A '''SilkPose_PR''' also has the following individual additional properties:

=== Data ===

{{Properties_Title|C1.1 - ref inputs}}

* {{PropertyData|position_ref|LinkSub}}: The subObject (vertex) used to define position.
* {{PropertyData|rotation_ref|Link}}: The Object used to define rotation.

{{Properties_Title|C1.2 - direct inputs}}

* {{PropertyData|relative_axes|Enumeration}}: Default is {{value|XY}}. The relative orientation to the rotation reference (XY, XZ, or YZ).
* {{PropertyData|symbol_scale|Float}}: Default is {{value|20.0}}. The overall size of the 3D symbol.

{{Properties_Title|C3 - Identifiers}}

* {{PropertyData|object_type|String}}: Default is {{value|SilkPose_PR}}. The workbench class used to create this object.


A '''SilkPose_3P''' also has the following individual additional properties:

=== Data ===

{{Properties_Title|C1.1 - ref inputs}}

* {{PropertyData|O_ref|LinkSub}}: The subObject (vertex) used to define origin.
* {{PropertyData|X_ref|LinkSub}}: The subObject (vertex) used to define x direction.
* {{PropertyData|Y_ref|LinkSub}}: The subObject (vertex) used to define y direction.

{{Properties_Title|C1.2 - direct inputs}}

* {{PropertyData|swap_XY|Bool}}: Default is {{value|False}}. Swaps X and Y references.

{{Properties_Title|C1.3 - direct inputs}}

* {{PropertyData|flip_X|Bool}}: Default is {{value|False}}. Reverses the x direction.
* {{PropertyData|flip_Y|Bool}}: Default is {{value|False}}. Reverses the y direction.
* {{PropertyData|relative_axes|Enumeration}}: Default is {{value|XY}}. The relative orientation to the rotation reference (XY, XZ, or YZ).

{{Properties_Title|C1.4 - direct inputs}}

* {{PropertyData|symbol_scale|Float}}: Default is {{value|20.0}}. The overall size of the 3D symbol.

{{Properties_Title|C3 - Identifiers}}

* {{PropertyData|object_type|String}}: Default is {{value|SilkPose_3P}}. The workbench class used to create this object.


